  "grade_cd_conclusion": "No inspected dataset provides explicit Grade A/B/C/D labels on individual nuts. The alwyndsouza21092 datasets provide real VIA bounding boxes, but every box is the single class areca_fruit: they can train a nut localizer, not a grade classifier. Their class_0...class_6 classification folders are undocumented and are not mapped to grades. The older datasets are image-level ripeness/plant-disease folders. Grade C/D cannot be trained from these files without fabricating labels. The current GradeA/GradeB detector is preserved. To enable C/D, annotate individual nuts with YOLO boxes labelled GradeA/GradeB/GradeC/GradeD, put the dataset in datasets/arecanut_grades (see datasets/README.md), then run scripts/prepare_dataset.py, scripts/train_model.py and scripts/evaluate_model.py."
